Question text:
Consider the following program fragment for reversing the digits in a given integer to obtain a new integer. Let $n = d_1 d_2 \ldots d_m$.

```c
int n, rev;
rev = 0;
while (n > 0) {
    rev = rev * 10 + n % 10;
    n = n / 10;
}
```

The loop invariant condition at the end of the $j^{th}$ iteration is:
(A) $n = d_1 d_2 \ldots d_{m-j}$ and $rev = d_m d_{m-1} \ldots d_{m-j+1}$
(B) $n = d_{m-j+1} \ldots d_{m-1} d_m$ or $rev = d_{m-j} \ldots d_2 d_1$
(C) $n \neq rev$
(D) $n = d_1 d_2 \ldots d_m$ or $rev = d_m \ldots d_2 d_1$

